<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  PLAYER overflow menu (G2).

  Source: canonical `Menu / Плеер` 2444:18763 (206x264, r20, `menuSurface` on a
  1px `menuOutline`), widened to 260 by the frozen proposal
  `sleep-timer-menu-active` 2517:2093 whose note is explicit - "The canonical menu
  is 206 wide, which cannot hold a label plus a trailing value. Widened to 260.
  This is the only change proposed to the existing menu."

  ## One row, not four

  The frozen menu has four: Найти трек, Таймер сна, Сообщить о проблеме, История
  эфира. Only the sleep timer exists, and this draws only the sleep timer.

  Four rows with three disabled was rejected for the reason G1 recorded when it
  left the whole overflow unbuilt and `SettingsLayoutTest` still holds: an inert
  row is tolerable when it names a feature the app genuinely has and cannot reach
  yet - `Row / Аватар` on profile-authenticated - and is not tolerable when it
  names a feature with no implementation behind it at all. Three greyed rows would
  be three dead controls stating that something exists.

  G1's own objection to drawing this menu was that it would be "a menu with one
  *unrelated* row" - it was being asked to carry Настройки, which is not one of the
  player's actions. Таймер сна is one of the four. That is why the slot opens now
  and did not open then, and it is the same rule the COLLECTION overflow lives
  under: a menu carries its own screen's actions and nothing else.

  The remaining three rows arrive with the slices that make them true.

  ## Geometry

  All of it from screens-3.6.6/spec/primitives.mjs:184, which is the frozen menu
  primitive both menus are authored on:

      menu            260 wide, r20, 10 top pad, 50 bottom pad (see below)
      row             238x48 at x=11, pitch 52
      icon slot       48 at x=12 in the row, 24 glyph centred in it
      label           x=70, 15/22 Medium
      trailing        x=160, w=70, 14/20 on `primary`

  ## One number here is temporary, and it is the only one

  The frozen bottom padding is **50** - stated in that file and reproduced by the
  two-row `Menu / Коллекция` at 260x160. This menu ships **10 / 10** while it
  carries a single row, by owner decision: the 50 is the complete four-row menu's
  geometry, and under one row it is 40 of unexplained space below a single 48dp
  line. The container hugs the row it has; every other frozen number - width, row
  box, pitch, radius, typography, colour - is unchanged.

  **Restoring it is part of shipping the next Player action.**
  `SleepTimerSurfacesTest` measures 10/10 and the resulting 68dp height, so a
  second row arriving without the padding being restored fails there rather than
  landing quietly.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/player_overflow_root"
    android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_width"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    android:background="@drawable/bg_player_overflow_menu"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:paddingTop="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_pad_top"
    android:paddingBottom="@dimen/player_overflow_menu_pad_bottom">

    <!-- `Menu row / Таймер сна`, the second row of the frozen four and the only
         one whose feature exists. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_row_height"
        android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:layout_marginEnd="@dimen/player_overflow_row_inset"
        android:background="?attr/selectableItemBackground"
        android:clickable="true"
        android:focusable="true"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:paddingStart="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot_inset"
        android:paddingEnd="0dp">

        <ImageView
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot"
            android:layout_height="@dimen/player_overflow_icon_slot"
            android:contentDescription="@null"
            android:scaleType="center"
            android:src="@drawable/ic_sleep_timer_clock" />

        <!--
          Label at x=70 in a row whose content starts at 12: the 48 slot ends at
          60, so the frozen gap is 10. Width is what is left after the trailing
          value's 70 - the frozen `w - 22 - 70 - 70` = 98 on a 260 menu - and the
          value is GONE rather than INVISIBLE when the timer is off, so the label
          takes the full 160 the frozen no-trailing rows have.
        -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer_label"
            android:layout_width="0dp"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="@dimen/player_overflow_gap"
            android:layout_weight="1"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:text="@string/sleep_timer_title"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Medium.15_22"
            android:textColor="@color/text_primary" />

        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/player_overflow_sleep_timer_trailing"
            android:layout_width="@dimen/player_overflow_trailing_width"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:ellipsize="end"
            android:maxLines="1"
            android:textAppearance="@style/TextAppearance.Myata.Onest.Regular.14_20"
            android:textColor="@color/primary"
            android:visibility="gone"
            tools:text="24 мин"
            tools:visibility="visible" />
    </LinearLayout>
</LinearLayout>
